{
  "text": "This paper proposes video diffusion models that keep the standard diffusion objective but replace the 2D U-Net with a space-time factorized 3D U-Net: space-only convolutions, spatial attention, then temporal attention with relative position embeddings. [@chk-b8e99140934e07b55f9bc037] For conditional generation (autoregressive extension, interpolation, or super-resolution) it introduces reconstruction-guided sampling: an adjusted denoiser that adds a weighted gradient on the model's reconstruction of the conditioning data, which the authors call reconstruction guidance. [@chk-55ff14777986cc7ded518ad1]",
  "citations": [
    {
      "chunk_id": "chk-55ff14777986cc7ded518ad1"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "chk-b8e99140934e07b55f9bc037"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "markdown": "Video diffusion models here jointly generate a fixed block of frames with a 3D U-Net that factorizes space and time, so the same network can be masked to train on independent images as well as video. [@chk-b8e99140934e07b55f9bc037]\n\nThe authors further introduce reconstruction-guided conditional sampling, which they report outperforms replacement/imputation when extending sequences by interpolation or autoregressive extrapolation, and they also use joint image-video training and classifier-free guidance. [@chk-46a2b47ca3da2a70f18055a9]",
  "citations": [
